  "determination": false,
  "rationale": "The example is only partly covered. The `habeas info` half is covered, but the `habeas status` half is not.\n\n**Info half: covered.** `info_renders_exact_and_glob_matches_as_markdown_without_an_index` (tests/commands.rs ~460) runs `habeas info requirements.*`. The fixture has requirements (`pending`, `ready`, `xready`) and the example `requirements.case`. The test asserts that both kinds appear, in full-name order. It also checks the \"Example\" and \"Requirement\" sections and the separator. This matches the \"displays both\" outcome.\n\n**Status half: not covered.** The example says `habeas status 'foo.*' --all` lists both the requirement and the example, with their kinds and evidence states. No test marked `{test}` for this example does that.\n- `status_and_info_accept_a_definition_selection` (tests/commands.rs ~701) runs `status requirements.c* --all`. That glob matches only the example `requirements.case`. The test asserts `| requirements.case (example)` and that `requirements.ready` is absent. It never shows a single glob returning a requirement and an example together, and it asserts no evidence-state values.\n- `commands_report_invalid_arguments_and_unmatched_selectors` (~524) does check that `status requirements.*ready --all` lists two requirements with the \"(requirement)\" label. It is not marked as a test of this example, and it contains no example.\n- `status_lists_nonvalid_requirements_and_all_option_in_name_order` (~367) checks the example's \"(example)\" label with no selection. It also is not marked for this example.\n\nSo no marked test covers the scenario of one glob with `--all` listing a requirement and an example with kinds and evidence states. Two `{test}` references exist, but the status assertions fall short of the example's stated outcome. Per the criteria this is a gap, and no FIXME acknowledges it.",
